{products.map((product) => (
  <>
    <ProductCard_DP
      key={product.id}
      product={product}
    />
    <ProductCard_P
      key={product.id}
      product={product}
    />
  </>
))}

⚠️ Works and UI displays, but not the correct key placement.
map() returns a Fragment <>...</>, but the key is placed on its child components instead of the Fragment.
Drawback: React may show the warning “Each child in a list should have a unique key prop”, because the Fragment itself has no key.

{products.map((product) => (
  <React.Fragment key={product.id}>
    <ProductCard_DP product={product} />
    <ProductCard_P product={product} />
  </React.Fragment>
))}

{products.map((product) => (
  <Fragment key={product.id}>
    <ProductCard_DP product={product} />
    <ProductCard_P product={product} />
  </Fragment>
))}

{products.map((product) => (
  <div key={product.id}>
    <ProductCard_DP product={product} />
    <ProductCard_P product={product} />
  </div>
))}

✅ Correct and recommended.
map() returns a React.Fragment, so key={product.id} is correctly placed on the Fragment.
Drawback: No key-related drawback. This is the proper way to return multiple components for each product without adding an extra <div>.

When map() returns multiple elements, put the key on the outermost element that wraps those elements — usually a Fragment or a div.

One component :-
map() → ProductCard       ➔ key on ProductCard ✅

Multiple components :-
map() → Fragment          ➔ key on Fragment ✅

Multiple components :-
map() → div               ➔ key on div ✅

JSX element can represent either an HTML element (<h1>, <div>, <p>, <span>, <button>, <input>, <ul>, <li>) or a React components (<ProductCard_P />, <ProductCard_DP />).

ProductCard	➔ Component Name
<ProductCard />	➔ JSX Element representing a React component
<div> ➔ HTML Element or JSX Element representing a React component

Single JSX element :-
map(product => (
  <ProductCard />
))

Multiple JSX elements in <div>...</div> :-
map(product => (
  <div>
    <ProductCard_DP />
    <ProductCard_P />
  </div>
))

Multiple JSX elements in Fragment <>...</> :-
map(product => (
  <>
    <ProductCard_DP />
    <ProductCard_P />
  </>
))

Multiple HTML elements inside a <div>...</div> :-
{products.map((product) => (
  <div key={product.id}>
    <h3>{product.name}</h3>
    <p>Price: ₹{product.price}</p>
    <button>Add to Cart</button>
  </div>
))}
